From c133ce5ef47436db7b18759db17ad5dfa0886e4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:11:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] cuda : narrower tiles in the sm_60 expert GEMM for
 short prompts

The expert GEMM tiles were 64 pairs wide; a 512-token batch gives an expert ~16 pairs, so three quarters of a tile
were padding. The tile width is now a template parameter (64 / 32 / 16) chosen from the average pairs per expert
(>= 40: 64, >= 12: 32, else 16). Every output is still summed by one thread in the same order: results unchanged.

q4_K gate, 256 experts x 8 used: 256 tokens 3300 -> 1832 us, 512 tokens 3404 -> 2353 us, 1024 tokens 3553 -> 3405 us.
2x P100 prefill: pp256 760, pp512 910 -> 970, pp1024 1128, pp4096 1578 t/s.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
